Small Fortune — third-party data notices
========================================

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the software. The curated price data under
`src/data/baskets/` is a separate work with the terms below. If you reuse that
data, these attributions travel with it.

Each item in a basket records where its price came from, in its `source`
field, so the obligations below can be traced per row rather than assumed
across the whole dataset.


1. Curated baskets — original compilation
-----------------------------------------
Rows marked `source: "local-survey"` and `source: "operator-published"` are an
original compilation, hand-assembled for this project from menus, public
listings, operator fare tables, national statistics releases and news
reporting. Individual prices are facts and are not themselves copyrightable;
the selection and arrangement are this project's own work.

Some baskets are marked `estimated: true`, meaning their absolute price levels
were derived from verified exchange-rate anchors and domain knowledge rather
than sourced local prices. They are indicative and are surfaced as such in the
interface. Do not present them as surveyed figures.


2. The Big Mac Index — CC BY 4.0
--------------------------------
Rows marked `source: "economist-bmi"` are derived from The Economist's Big Mac
Index.

    Source:  https://github.com/TheEconomist/big-mac-data
    Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
             https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    Credit:  The Economist

Reuse requires attribution to The Economist and an indication of whether
changes were made. Values here are taken as published, in local currency, from
the index release named in the accompanying commentary.


3. WFP food prices via HDX — CC BY 3.0 IGO
------------------------------------------
The `wfp-hdx` source is declared and available for staple-food rows.

    Source:  https://data.humdata.org/dataset/global-wfp-food-prices
    Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 IGO (CC BY 3.0 IGO)
             https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/igo/
    Credit:  World Food Programme

No item currently draws on this dataset — HDX was unreachable when the baskets
were built. This notice is kept in place so the obligation is already recorded
if and when those rows are sourced.


4. Exchange rates — attribution required
----------------------------------------
Live rates come from ExchangeRate-API's open-access endpoint, whose terms
require visible attribution. A credit link appears in the site footer; keep it
if you deploy this.

    Provider: https://www.exchangerate-api.com
    Terms:    https://www.exchangerate-api.com/terms

A fallback provider is used when the primary is unreachable:

    Provider: https://github.com/fawazahmed0/exchange-api


5. Deliberately not used
------------------------
Numbeo is not a source for any row, at any tier. Its terms prohibit automated
collection, its free tier does not cover a public product, and a paid licence
still forbids redistributing the data through a public-facing feed.

Widely-mirrored "global cost of living" datasets labelled CC0 on data-sharing
sites are, in the cases reviewed, Numbeo scrapes relabelled by uploaders with
no standing to relicense them. That badge is not clearance. None were used
here, and none should be merged into this dataset.


